      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1123,
      "output": "Water is a chemical substance that is essential for life on Earth. It is most commonly known by its chemical formula, **$H_2O$**.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is made of and why it is unique:\n\n### 1. Chemical Composition\nWater is a **compound**, meaning it is made by chemically bonding two or more different elements together.\n*   **2 Hydrogen atoms:** These are light, gaseous elements.\n*   **1 Oxygen atom:** This is a heavy, reactive gas.\n*   When these three atoms bond together, they form a water molecule.\n\n### 2. Physical States\nWater is unique because it can exist naturally in all three states of matter at standard temperatures and pressures:\n*   **Solid:** When frozen, it is called **ice**.\n*   **Liquid:** This is the state we see most often (rain, oceans, drinking water).\n*   **Gas:** When heated, it turns into water vapor or steam.\n\n### 3. Key Properties\nWater has several unique physical and chemical properties that make it vital for life:\n*   **Polarity:** The oxygen atom pulls electrons away from the hydrogen atoms, giving water a slight negative charge on one side and a slight positive charge on the other. This allows water molecules to stick to each other (cohesion) and to other surfaces (adhesion).\n*   **The Universal Solvent:** Water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it is the main transport system in the human body (carrying nutrients) and in nature (carrying minerals in rivers).\n*   **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat without getting hot. This helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps human bodies from overheating.\n\n### 4. Biological Importance\nWater is the primary component of all living things. Humans are about 60% water, and it is required for:\n*   Digestion\n*   Temperature regulation (sweating)\n*   Lubricating joints\n*   Transporting oxygen and nutrients to cells"
